          "text": "CLINICAL INDICATION: Focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at age 29, occurring approximately twice yearly. Structural etiology; drug responsive. Current antiseizure medications: zonisamide and oxcarbazepine.\n\nTECHNIQUE: Multiplanar, multisequence MRI of the brain was performed using an epilepsy protocol, including high-resolution coronal imaging through the temporal lobes.\n\nFINDINGS: Hippocampal volume loss, increased T2/FLAIR signal, and loss of normal internal architecture are present, consistent with hippocampal sclerosis.\n\nIMPRESSION: Hippocampal sclerosis.",
